  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Kripa Shankar Paswan And Anr vs Mcd And Ors on 4 September, 2023 Author: Siddharth Mridul Bench: Siddharth Mridul #S-43 In The High Court Of Delhi At New Delhi Judgment Delivered On: 0 W.P.(C) 11584/2023 Kripa Shankar Paswan And Anr .. Versus Municipal Corporaton Of Delhi & ORS.....Respondents Advocates who appeared in this case: For the Petitioners : Mr. Anjani Kumar Mishra, Mr. Kamlesh Mr. Aditya, Mr. Bibhuti Bhushan Mish Raj and Mr. Kailash Kr. Jha, Advocat For the Respondents : Ms. Vandana Sehgal, Advocate for R-1 Mr. Sanjay Lao, Standing Counsel (Cr 4/Sho, P.S.: Laxmi Nagar. Coram: Hon'Ble Mr. Justice Siddharth Mridul Hon'Ble Mr. Justice Anish Dayal Judgment",
    "facts": "Pass an order directing the respondent MCD to correct the nomenclature in the column for Type of Vendor from \"Food/Snacks with gas cylinder/fire\" to \"Stationary Street Vendor\" (in view of the Section 6 of the Act) as detailed in the vending certificates issued to the petitioners.",
    "arguments": "8. Vendor/Squatter shall insure that no hindrance be caused to pedestrian and vehicular moment. Learned counsel appearing on behalf of the petitioners states, that they do not pray for the relief of running their business from any particular vending site, within the zone where they have been permitted to vend by the Municipal Corporation of Delhi, and further, the limited relief that is prayed for, is to permit the petitioners to vend strictly, in accordance with the terms and conditions of the Certificates of Vending dated 08.11.2021, issued by the Municipal Corporation of Delhi. 7.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "Learned counsel appearing on behalf of the petitioners states, that they do not pray for the relief of running their business from any particular vending site, within the zone where they have been permitted to vend by the Municipal Corporation of Delhi, and further, the limited relief that is prayed for, is to permit the petitioners to vend strictly, in accordance with the terms and conditions of the Certificates of Vending dated 08.11.2021, issued by the Municipal Corporation of Delhi. 7.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": "8. Vendor/Squatter shall insure that no hindrance be caused to pedestrian and vehicular moment."
  },
